    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A property with huge potential in an attractive price bracket, St Philomena's is a fine 3-bedroom, detached bungalow nestled in the mature and sought after surroundings of Fairgreen, just a short stroll from the main street in Rathdrum.\n\nWhile the property does require modernisation and renovation, it represents an exciting opportunity for first-time buyers, downsizers, or investors to create a bespoke dream home in a fantastic location. With its generous layout, excellent footprint, and proximity to the main street and all its amenities, St Philomenas is a little gem with endless potential. There is a spacious front garden with ample parking, a private, south west-facing rear garden and a large garage adjoining the house which is ideal for any number of uses—all situated in a superb location just a short walk from Rathdrum Main Street.\n\nAccommodation Comprises:\nEntrance Hall, Living Room, Kitchen, Sitting Room, Family Bathroom, Bedroom 1, Bedroom 2, Bedroom 3.\nHeating is via an oil-fired central heating system. There is double glazing to the front and single glazing to the rear.\n\nSt Philomenas sits on a rectangular site of c 0.15 acres The gardens have been landscaped and well maintained. The property has mains water, sewerage and electricity. The bungalow is situated in a quiet residential setting close to the main street of Rathdrum, within walking distance of all local amenities including, shops, pubs, restaurants, schools etc. \n\nRathdrum has everything you could want for a modern lifestyle; excellent schools, great shopping, wonderful restaurants and pubs, as well as a huge variety of outdoor activities. This growing town enjoys excellent transport links to Dublin and is well serviced by both rail, bus and road. The M11 motorway is 15 minutes away and South Dublin and the M50 are within 40 minutes drive. Alternatively, commuters can avail of the rail line which runs to Connolly Station via Wicklow, Greystones, and Bray. Rathdrum is beautifully situated on the western side of the stunning Avonmore Valley, in the heart of the Garden of Ireland, close to the majestic Wicklow Mountains, and the beautiful Wicklow coastline. The Vale of Avoca, Glendalough, The Meeting of the Waters and Brittas Bay are all within a short drive.\n\nContact Stephen Clarke today to arrange a viewing on 087 2051659."
      },
